  "id": "DrugBank_DB11992 - MONDO_5015",
  "verbalization": "Omarigliptin is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the indication of the drug for diabetes. The evidence suggests that Omarigliptin is classified under the broader category of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, and this condition is linked to several drugs, including Albiglutide, Gemigliptin, and Teneligliptin. These drugs are all indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, creating a chain of indications that connects Omarigliptin to the disease. The shared indication for diabetes mellitus across these drugs implies a potential mechanism of action that targets the same biological pathways, possibly related to glucose regulation or insulin sensitivity. The high scores in the paths suggest that the relationship is well-supported, but the exact mechanism of how Omarigliptin interacts with these drugs to influence diabetes remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering drug indications and their associated conditions in the context of drug reutilization.",
